`pip-audit` has no precise license metadata field in the installed distribution; its packaged `licenses/LICENSE` identifies Apache License 2.0. `pip-tools` reports `BSD`; its packaged `licenses/LICENSE` identifies BSD 3-Clause. Extra dependencies selected by `uvicorn[standard]` belong to the transitive graph, not additional direct rows.

## Font Notices

The installed `@fontsource/cinzel/LICENSE` and `@fontsource/rajdhani/LICENSE` contain SIL Open Font License 1.1 and the following copyright notices. Preserve those license files and notices with redistributed font software.

Cinzel:

> Copyright 2020 The Cinzel Project Authors (https://github.com/NDISCOVER/Cinzel)

Rajdhani:

> Copyright (c) 2014 Indian Type Foundry (info@indiantypefoundry.com) Rajdhani-Regular.ttf: Copyright (c) 2014 Indian Type Foundry (info@indiantypefoundry.com) Rajdhani-Medium.ttf: Copyright (c) 2014 Indian Type Foundry (info@indiantypefoundry.com) Rajdhani-SemiBold.ttf: Copyright (c) 2014 Indian Type Foundry (info@indiantypefoundry.com) Rajdhani-Bold.ttf: Copyright (c) 2014 Indian Type Foundry (info@indiantypefoundry.com)

The production Dockerfile copies the installed production dependency tree, including these package license files, and `public/`. The font copyright notices and full OFL text are also in [public/third-party-notices.txt](public/third-party-notices.txt), served with the web assets. This source/configuration check does not claim a fresh built-container audit or complete coverage of other distribution formats.

## Remote Runtime Dependency

The character viewer loads jQuery 2.1.3 from `https://ajax.googleapis.com/ajax/libs/jquery/2.1.3/jquery.min.js`. It is outside the 42 direct package count. The [exact upstream version's MIT license](https://github.com/jquery/jquery/blob/2.1.3/MIT-LICENSE.txt) identifies Copyright 2014 jQuery Foundation and other contributors; its full notice is preserved in [public/third-party-notices.txt](public/third-party-notices.txt). The retrieved script on 2026-09-05 was 84,320 bytes with SHA-256 `8af93bd675e1cfd9ecc850e862819fdac6e3ad1f5d761f970e409c7d9c63bdc3`. This license does not cover the separate viewer or game media.

## Scope and Unresolved Rights

The lockfiles describe the transitive dependency graph. This update does not establish a complete transitive license review or verify every notice in built browser bundles and container layers.

Warcraft names, artwork, icons, models, video, audio, and other media are outside the dependency inventory. An MIT license on Pizza Logs source does not establish their rights. The site is not being sold or transferred, so acquisition clearance is not a current requirement; ordinary third-party usage terms still apply.

The current-file hashes, owner-attested Veo/ChatGPT origins, local generation chain, remote icon/model consumers and revised A16 scope are recorded in [Asset provenance and rights evidence](docs/security/asset-provenance.md). Unverified current-use details remain explicit; the register does not certify all media rights.

The UwU reference inspected at `4c046d266b85ad833ab4d70addb0b6f1a16647e3` has no detected general redistribution license. Its README permits self-hosting, which does not establish permission to copy or redistribute its implementation in Pizza Logs. Reference comparison and provenance are documented separately in `docs/uwu-analytics-parity.md`.

Refresh this inventory after dependency manifest or lockfile changes. License identifiers and retained notices are evidence for review, not a legal clearance conclusion.
